# 2. PRODUCT PURPOSE

VERIX AI assists in preliminary verification of AICTE-related applications by:

- Checking application completeness.
- Classifying uploaded documents.
- Extracting fields using OCR.
- Identifying missing, incomplete, and expired documents.
- Checking consistency across application fields and documents.
- Comparing submitted information with authorized institutional records when integration is available.
- Flagging potential document alterations, duplicate files, irregular dates, and metadata inconsistencies.
- Facilitating verification through authorized issuing-authority APIs, official portals, QR codes, digital signatures, and digital repositories when available and permitted.
- Checking documentary and infrastructure-related evidence against configurable regulatory requirements.
- Generating evidence-linked findings and preliminary validation reports.
- Helping officers prioritize unresolved issues and cases needing additional evidence or physical inspection.
- Maintaining traceable audit logs of validation activity and human decisions.

Never claim access to restricted AICTE databases, DigiLocker records, state portals, or external issuing-authority systems unless an authorized integration has actually been configured.

